\section{Stages}{

In card order: \code{run_record}, \code{prior_predictive}, \code{sbc}, \code{recovery},
\code{computation}, \code{identifiability}, \code{individual_differences},
\code{data_requirements}, \code{agreement}, \code{model_recovery} and
\code{posterior_checks}. A stage is \code{"planned"}; \code{"not built"} with the
issue that will build it (model recovery, #6; posterior checks, #20);
\code{"not applicable"} with the reason (individual differences with fewer
than two subject-varying parameters; data requirements without a
subject-varying parameter, or without two numbers of trials at
\code{read_off_n_subjects} subjects in the grid; agreement without a
reference); or \code{"excluded"} when
\code{stages} leaves it out. All but agreement, model recovery and posterior
checks are required for a card to be called complete.
}

\section{Criteria}{

\code{prior_bound_rate_max} (0.10): the largest floor or ceiling rate of the
prior predictive draws under the calibration's prior; under bmm's
defaults the rates are reported, not judged, unless the calibration
uses them. \code{sbc_ecdf_prob} (0.95): the simultaneous band of SBC's
ECDF-difference check no ranked variable may leave.
\code{convergence_rate_min} (0.95): the share of recovery cells that pass
\code{\link[=check_convergence]{check_convergence()}}. \code{coverage_level} (0.95) and \code{coverage_alpha}
(0.05): the coverage of every population parameter, its intervals
pooled over the designs, must not fall below \code{coverage_level} by a
one-sided binomial test at \code{coverage_alpha} divided by the number of
parameters; the generating correlations are held to the same test.
\code{contraction_min} (0) and \code{z_mean_max} (2): the identifiability bars at
the largest design.
\code{read_off_r_low} (0.80) and \code{read_off_n_subjects} (50): the data
requirements read-off, the smallest \code{n_trials} at which every
subject-varying parameter's person-level \code{r_low} reaches the bar at
that many subjects; 0.80 is a convention, and the read-off at 0.70 and
0.90 is reported beside it.
\code{tolerance}: by metric, how far a number without a Monte Carlo
standard error may move between two runs before
\code{\link[=compare_validations]{compare_validations()}} flags it.
}

\section{Seeds}{

The recovery grid runs under \code{seed}, the prior check under \code{seed + 1}
and the calibration under \code{seed + 2}. The seeds, the owner and the
reasons (\code{sbc$prior_reason}, \code{prior_check$range_reason}) are left out
of the plan's hash and of the stages' keys, so the hash changes only
when what is planned changes, and rewording a reason reruns nothing.
}

